pothesis-templates.ts\n.pi/duet/runs/2026-03-21T04-43-48-951Z-726f17fc/steps/2\n\nYour session has context from prior steps. The repository may have changed since your last turn.\nBefore making assumptions about file contents, verify the current state of any files you need to modify.\nDo NOT re-read files that are unrelated to the current step.\n\nStep 3: 7.10 — Enhance node resource investigation with capacity, taints, and pod correlation (TDD)\n{\n  \"id\": \"step-3\",\n  \"title\": \"7.10 — Enhance node resource investigation with capacity, taints, and pod correlation (TDD)\",\n  \"description\": \"Node conditions (NotReady, MemoryPressure, DiskPressure, PIDPressure) and seeds already exist. What's missing: (a) node resource capacity vs allocatable analysis to detect over-committed nodes, (b) taint analysis to detect unschedulable taints that explain pod scheduling failures, (c) correlation between node pressure conditions and OOMKilled pods running on that node.\\n\\n**TDD tests first** in `src/investigators/__tests__/kubernetes-investigator.test.ts`:\\n1. Test: Node with allocatable memory significantly lower than capacity → finding about node resource constraint.\\n2. Test: Node with `NoSchedule` taint and pods stuck in Pending → causal edge linking taint to scheduling failure.\\n3. Test: Node with MemoryPressure and pods on that node OOMKilled → causal edge from node pressure to OOM finding.\\n4. Test: Healthy node (all conditions OK, no taints, normal capacity) → no additional findings.\\n\\nAlso add seeds tests in `seed-generator.test.ts`:\\n5. Test: Node with taints that prevent scheduling generates a seed.\\n\\n**Implementation:**\\n1. In `kubernetes-investigator.ts`, add `investigateNodeResources(context, counter)` function:\\n   - Extract `status.allocatable` and `status.capacity` from Node resources.\\n   - When allocatable memory < 80% of capacity, emit a `medium` finding about node resource constraints.\\n   - Extract `spec.taints` from Node resources. For each `NoSchedule` or `NoExecute` taint, check if any Pending pods have matching tolerations. If a pod lacks a required toleration, emit a finding with a causal edge.\\n2. In `investigateNodeConditions`, add correlation: when a node has MemoryPressure=True, scan for OOMKilled containers on pods assigned to that node (`spec.nodeName`). Create causal edges from the MemoryPressure finding to OOM findings.\\n3. Wire `investigateNodeResources` into the public `investigateKubernetes` function.\\n4. In `seed-generator.ts`, extend `seedsFromNodes` to also emit seeds for nodes with `NoSchedule` taints.\",\n  \"requiredChecks\": [\n    \"lint\",\n    \"typecheck\",\n    \"unit\",\n    \"build\"\n  ]\n}\n\nYou are the first agent to work on this step.\nImplement the changes described above, run checks to verify, and fix any issues before handing off.\nBe thorough — the next agent will review your work and should find it correct.\n\nWhen done, explain what you reviewed, what you changed (if anything), and your assessment.\n\nEnd with:\nVerdict: approve  — if the step is complete and correct, no more changes needed\nVerdict: changes_made  — if you made fixes or improvements\nVerdict: replan_needed  — if the step is structurally impossible to complete as planned and needs controller-managed replanning"}],"timestamp":1774101423892}}
